1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,617
Stand up tall, reach out your hand.

2
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:06,797
Cut through the wind and make a stand!

3
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:11,240
The paint within brings
out a map of your own.

4
00:00:16,020 --> 00:00:19,597
To the left and the right,
all we saw stormy nights?

5
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:22,877
All the rough winds and
waves coming day after day!

6
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:28,777
And the values we had were about to
collapse Oh just where do we go next?

7
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:35,440
And as we look down to the compass in
hand Is it showing us the right direction?

8
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:38,617
All we know is nobody
here knows it for certain.

9
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:41,937
So close your eyes and breathe in deeply.

10
00:00:42,020 --> 00:00:45,237
And listen to your soul.

11
00:00:45,320 --> 00:00:48,117
You'll see a path in front of you.

12
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:51,537
And you'll know just where you need to go.

13
00:00:51,620 --> 00:00:55,817
So stand up tall, reach out your hand.

14
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:59,037
Cut through the wind and make us stand.

15
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:02,900
Don't let the darkness
win, just break through.

16
00:01:04,620 --> 00:01:08,137
I'll do it my own way,
that's what's best for me.

17
00:01:08,220 --> 00:01:11,777
And you do it your way,
that's how it's got to be.

18
00:01:11,860 --> 00:01:15,357
We're moving forward, now I'm ready.

19
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:19,217
But at times it's okay
to get help on the way.

20
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:21,777
For the future ahead, burning bright.

21
00:01:21,860 --> 00:01:24,197
For what's ahead you see.

22
00:01:24,280 --> 00:01:27,620
Is beyond your wildest dreams.

23
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:31,757
So stand up tall, reach out your hand.

24
00:01:31,840 --> 00:01:34,977
Cut through the wind and make a stand.

25
00:01:35,060 --> 00:01:38,840
Don't let the darkness
win, just break through.

26
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:44,097
We'll do it our way the best that we know.

27
00:01:44,180 --> 00:01:45,557
With tears and doubts and tone.

28
00:01:45,640 --> 00:01:47,917
We'll go where we all wanna go.

29
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,720
The page within brings colors of our own.

30
00:02:05,440 --> 00:02:10,520
I am waiting for you, Momonosuke.

31
00:02:11,700 --> 00:02:15,640
I am waiting for your order.

32
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:22,920
Far have I traveled to stand beside you.

33
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:29,640
Now in your moment of need,
I will fight in your name.

34
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:33,580
I was able to speak with
Zunisha for a moment at least.

35
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:36,280
So you can talk to the elephant.

36
00:02:36,940 --> 00:02:38,940
Odin predicted this years ago.

37
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:42,071
You're everything he dreamed you would be.

38
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:43,700
You've got this!

39
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:47,280
And you'll lead this world to a new dawn!

40
00:02:48,780 --> 00:02:52,309
We're still missing the most
important piece of this puzzle.

41
00:02:54,160 --> 00:02:58,866
After reading Father's journal, I understand
that I must survive no matter what.

42
00:02:59,740 --> 00:03:01,240
But I'm still lost.

43
00:03:02,060 --> 00:03:05,942
Because he tore out the most
important page before I could see it!

44
00:03:08,980 --> 00:03:09,810
Laugh Tale.

45
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:12,080
The final island.

46
00:03:14,460 --> 00:03:16,840
What did Father and Roger see there?

47
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:18,740
What made them laugh?

48
00:03:24,320 --> 00:03:27,100
I struggle to understand my mission.

49
00:03:28,700 --> 00:03:30,420
Father was not a prophet.

50
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:33,257
If he were here now,

51
00:03:33,340 --> 00:03:37,105
would he still insist on opening
the borders like he did before?

52
00:03:38,420 --> 00:03:41,037
I have not the wisdom to solve this.

53
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:44,700
If opening the borders puts
the people of Wano in danger,

54
00:03:44,980 --> 00:03:47,360
then I do not want to do it!

55
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:51,997
Am I a coward, Yamato?

56
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:52,960
Tell me!

57
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:04,980
Charret, get inside the dome!

58
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:10,060
We have taken our revenge, but I fear
the battle for Wano is far from over.

59
00:04:10,660 --> 00:04:11,797
Hey!

60
00:04:11,880 --> 00:04:12,780
I'm ready!

61
00:04:13,140 --> 00:04:14,340
Let's go help out!

62
00:04:15,480 --> 00:04:18,097
Seems this island can
collapse at any moment.

63
00:04:18,180 --> 00:04:19,651
We had better hurry them.

64
00:04:20,720 --> 00:04:22,080
I got you, bro!

65
00:04:22,300 --> 00:04:23,140
Hold on!

66
00:04:24,220 --> 00:04:26,161
Really put your life on the line.

67
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:28,379
It's getting roughed up, aren't ya?

68
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:29,680
Stay steady!

69
00:04:29,980 --> 00:04:31,215
I'm gonna reel ya in!

70
00:04:32,840 --> 00:04:33,670
Hey!

71
00:04:33,820 --> 00:04:35,349
You're still alive, right?

72
00:04:35,920 --> 00:04:36,960
Say something!

73
00:04:38,940 --> 00:04:40,900
You better not be dead, bro!

74
00:04:42,320 --> 00:04:43,150
Zoro!

75
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:48,160
I won't let you die.

76
00:04:48,540 --> 00:04:50,140
You gotta stay with me.

77
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:52,480
This is bad, really bad.

78
00:04:52,740 --> 00:04:54,975
The whole castle is about to collapse.

79
00:04:55,380 --> 00:04:57,556
Hamlet, get us to the exit and hurry!

80
00:04:58,020 --> 00:05:00,060
No need to worry, I will!

81
00:05:00,340 --> 00:05:03,117
Not to pressure you, but lives
are hanging in the balance.

82
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:06,200
If there's ever been a time
to deliver, this is it!

83
00:05:27,780 --> 00:05:29,437
The time has come.

84
00:05:29,520 --> 00:05:33,280
For even ninja like you and I To be free!

85
00:05:35,160 --> 00:05:39,380
The fiery battle in the third-floor
hallway has come to an end.

86
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:42,520
The winner, Race of the Mist.

87
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:49,860
Are you a samurai?

88
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:52,242
You need to get out of here now.

89
00:05:55,420 --> 00:05:58,860
You're a Gourmet of Sir
Luffy's, aren't you?

90
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:03,760
Let me aid you.

91
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:05,777
You're in no shape to fight, I fear.

92
00:06:05,860 --> 00:06:07,095
You have done enough.

93
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:08,140
I must try.

94
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:10,820
I can't rest till the battle is won.

95
00:06:11,080 --> 00:06:13,277
I won't let you march to your own death.

96
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:14,536
Then I need a favor.

97
00:06:36,220 --> 00:06:38,480
Finger Pistol?

98
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:54,620
Shift. Shake!

99
00:06:59,200 --> 00:07:00,030
Finger pistol!

100
00:07:10,200 --> 00:07:11,030
Finger pistol!

101
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:25,760
You have to live!

102
00:07:27,940 --> 00:07:28,880
Kiku!

103
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:40,630
Impossible.

104
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:45,430
Maha!

105
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:48,080
Was this your plan, Izo?

106
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:53,859
You were going to sacrifice
yourself from the start.

107
00:07:54,020 --> 00:07:58,257
Why would a leftover from the Whitebeard
Pirates want to help those brats?

108
00:07:58,340 --> 00:08:00,600
I must find Nico Robin quickly.

109
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:04,700
I don't have time to
deal with this right now.

110
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:07,780
Listen carefully.

111
00:08:08,220 --> 00:08:11,080
It's an Imperial command
from the Five Elders.

112
00:08:11,980 --> 00:08:12,810
What?

113
00:08:12,893 --> 00:08:13,860
From the Five Elders?

114
00:08:14,520 --> 00:08:19,480
They said, erase Straw
Hat Luffy immediately.

115
00:08:20,780 --> 00:08:23,133
Do you realize what you're asking of me?

116
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:26,029
Straw Hat is fighting
an emperor right now.

117
00:08:26,540 --> 00:08:29,837
You expect me just to step into
the middle of Kaido's fight?

118
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:31,038
That'll never work.

119
00:08:31,180 --> 00:08:32,320
Then make it work.

120
00:08:32,540 --> 00:08:34,020
It's the only option.

121
00:08:35,360 --> 00:08:39,654
The longer Straw Hat fights someone
of his caliber, the greater the risk.

122
00:08:39,860 --> 00:08:41,100
Don't you get it?

123
00:08:41,760 --> 00:08:44,900
The five elders call it
a necessary precaution.

124
00:08:46,660 --> 00:08:50,037
If they're worried about it,
then we know the rumors are true.

125
00:08:50,120 --> 00:08:55,340
At the very least, we don't want
to find out, understand? I'll wait.

126
00:08:58,520 --> 00:09:00,000
I can't die yet.

127
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:01,849
I've accomplished nothing.

128
00:09:04,060 --> 00:09:05,940
What's going on with that crew?

129
00:09:08,360 --> 00:09:11,040
What makes the Straw Hats so special?

130
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:21,620
Oh, Mathieu, thank you so much
for doing such a wonderful job.

131
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:28,100
You did it, boss!

132
00:09:28,700 --> 00:09:29,530
Captain!

133
00:09:31,860 --> 00:09:34,060
You did it from the sea!

134
00:09:34,460 --> 00:09:37,680
This is a big deal, a really big deal!

135
00:09:38,520 --> 00:09:40,932
Sounds like Big Mom won't be coming back.

136
00:09:41,560 --> 00:09:42,860
It's hard to believe.

137
00:09:44,040 --> 00:09:45,100
Mama, no!

138
00:09:48,560 --> 00:09:50,660
What are you crying about, Zeus?

139
00:09:50,920 --> 00:09:54,508
You don't need Big Mom anymore
now that you've got me, right?

140
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:56,780
Of course not, Ami!

141
00:10:01,020 --> 00:10:01,940
Master, here!

142
00:10:02,400 --> 00:10:03,640
Stay close to me!

143
00:10:04,200 --> 00:10:06,259
Looks like we can't relax just yet.

144
00:10:06,920 --> 00:10:08,757
We have to be ready for anything.

145
00:10:08,840 --> 00:10:12,500
This island is a bomb set to explode.

146
00:10:14,180 --> 00:10:18,000
Luffy I hope you can wrap this up soon.

147
00:10:33,560 --> 00:10:35,080
Why aren't you here?

148
00:10:35,840 --> 00:10:36,670
Fukurokuju!

149
00:10:37,340 --> 00:10:38,170
Oh,

150
00:10:38,253 --> 00:10:42,637
Kurosaki don't worry my dear we'll get
out of this accursed place soon enough

151
00:10:42,720 --> 00:10:46,777
useless ninja you're supposed to be

152
00:10:46,860 --> 00:10:51,317
helping me so what's the hold up huh that

153
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:55,537
bastard didn't run away on his own did
he a ninja must serve his Lord till the

154
00:10:55,620 --> 00:10:58,157
end if anyone's gonna die it should be him

155
00:10:58,240 --> 00:11:03,837
wonder who caused

156
00:11:03,920 --> 00:11:05,340
that quake conjurer oh

157
00:11:06,060 --> 00:11:06,890
Maybe.

158
00:11:06,973 --> 00:11:08,713
I sure hope there's not more on the way.

159
00:11:25,660 --> 00:11:26,490
Hey!

160
00:11:26,700 --> 00:11:27,540
That's enough!

161
00:11:28,700 --> 00:11:29,820
We're in danger!

162
00:11:30,320 --> 00:11:33,026
Why are you playing music
at a time like this?

163
00:11:34,560 --> 00:11:36,297
Are you listening to me?

164
00:11:36,380 --> 00:11:38,537
Stop this instant!

165
00:11:38,620 --> 00:11:41,497
Do you realize we're both
dead if we don't get help?

166
00:11:41,580 --> 00:11:44,600
And here you are wearing
that ridiculous mask.

167
00:11:50,240 --> 00:11:52,757
You haven't shown me
your face once have you?

168
00:11:52,840 --> 00:11:56,040
Take off that mask right now!

169
00:12:03,100 --> 00:12:05,980
You are Kurosaki, right?

170
00:12:06,140 --> 00:12:07,220
You have to be.

171
00:12:07,700 --> 00:12:09,980
Please say something.

172
00:12:11,660 --> 00:12:13,960
Are you a ghost?

173
00:12:15,320 --> 00:12:16,150
Oh.

174
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:43,060
Let's go.

175
00:13:02,900 --> 00:13:03,730
Stop!

176
00:13:17,560 --> 00:13:20,300
Have you noticed yet? Hey!

177
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:25,900
Those little bastards.

178
00:13:26,520 --> 00:13:28,140
They really did it.

179
00:13:32,900 --> 00:13:33,730
No!

180
00:13:33,813 --> 00:13:35,420
She's gone now!

181
00:13:36,400 --> 00:13:38,100
I'm in this way!

182
00:13:40,500 --> 00:13:42,340
Jackie and Traffy won?

183
00:13:42,600 --> 00:13:43,820
Wow, that's awesome!

184
00:13:49,900 --> 00:13:52,460
Should we get ready, Kaido might come.

185
00:13:54,560 --> 00:13:55,972
That would be pointless.

186
00:13:59,460 --> 00:14:02,260
Just hope it's Luffy
who comes back for us.

187
00:14:06,700 --> 00:14:08,360
My energy is all spent.

188
00:14:10,100 --> 00:14:11,920
I gave this everything I had.

189
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:14,220
I can't fight anymore.

190
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:21,620
Mama, mama.

191
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:24,040
Hey, brat!

192
00:14:24,840 --> 00:14:26,780
You know it's rude to stare!

193
00:14:28,300 --> 00:14:29,130
Hello?

194
00:14:30,980 --> 00:14:32,740
You got a mouth, don't you?

195
00:14:38,640 --> 00:14:42,117
How old are you, mama? mama!

196
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:43,457
15.

197
00:14:43,540 --> 00:14:44,917
So young.

198
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:48,817
This must be your first
time teaming up with rocks!

199
00:14:48,900 --> 00:14:50,797
Well, there's never a dull moment.

200
00:14:50,880 --> 00:14:54,577
I'll warn you, rocks
is a good for nothing.

201
00:14:54,660 --> 00:14:57,537
You can't trust a word he says.

202
00:14:57,620 --> 00:14:58,777
You got a problem?

203
00:14:58,860 --> 00:15:02,357
You bring it to me, mama! mama!

204
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:08,577
The name's linlin and don't you forget it.

205
00:15:08,660 --> 00:15:10,557
I'm gonna be king of these seas.

206
00:15:10,640 --> 00:15:13,237
Welcome to the team!

207
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:18,337
Looking back,

208
00:15:18,420 --> 00:15:23,517
you and I have known each other
an awfully long time, haven't we?

209
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:25,597
You old hack!

210
00:15:25,680 --> 00:15:27,257
It's not fair!

211
00:15:27,340 --> 00:15:29,680
Why does that have to happen now?

212
00:15:33,820 --> 00:15:36,117
We made a promise together.

213
00:15:36,200 --> 00:15:40,600
We were gonna get the one piece!

214
00:15:46,100 --> 00:15:47,340
Fourth gear.

215
00:16:10,120 --> 00:16:12,940
I have a moment of silence.

216
00:16:13,300 --> 00:16:16,240
This is a very emotional time for me.

217
00:16:16,740 --> 00:16:18,437
Read the damn room.

218
00:16:18,520 --> 00:16:21,300
I can't move.

219
00:16:24,640 --> 00:16:26,060
I'm trapped here.

220
00:16:27,600 --> 00:16:29,460
How careless of you.

221
00:16:30,120 --> 00:16:34,040
You got so worked up that
you didn't even notice.

222
00:16:34,360 --> 00:16:37,300
Gomorrah Saki, why aren't you helping?

223
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:39,780
Get this damn rubble off of me.

224
00:16:40,420 --> 00:16:41,860
Something is wrong.

225
00:16:42,520 --> 00:16:44,080
I feel so weak.

226
00:16:44,260 --> 00:16:45,554
Why can't I transform?

227
00:16:46,280 --> 00:16:47,660
Of course you can't.

228
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:52,140
I couldn't have you using your power,

229
00:16:52,440 --> 00:16:58,120
after all, so I stuck a sea prism
stone nail in you, to keep you docile.

230
00:16:59,500 --> 00:17:00,580
But why?

231
00:17:00,960 --> 00:17:02,920
None of this makes any sense.

232
00:17:03,200 --> 00:17:05,141
We were going to escape together.

233
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:07,459
You mean you don't love me anymore?

234
00:17:08,860 --> 00:17:09,690
Anymore?

235
00:17:09,840 --> 00:17:11,057
How amusing.

236
00:17:11,140 --> 00:17:13,680
I never loved you in the first place.

237
00:17:17,520 --> 00:17:20,997
It's quite a coincidence that
you like this piece so much.

238
00:17:21,080 --> 00:17:24,220
It's called Moon Princess.

239
00:17:26,120 --> 00:17:27,997
That's beautiful, Hiyori.

240
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:30,920
You've gotten so good at playing. Really?

241
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:35,660
The song's called Moon Princess
I'm gonna try to get even better.

242
00:17:39,040 --> 00:17:40,757
Good, keep it up!

243
00:17:40,840 --> 00:17:43,220
You can play it at my funeral someday.

244
00:17:48,780 --> 00:17:52,357
Hey momo, stop making your sister cry!

245
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:54,237
You're the one who made her cry.

246
00:17:54,320 --> 00:18:00,200
Me, the funeral thing, I'm
sorry, it was only a joke.

247
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:01,910
Promise?

248
00:18:04,160 --> 00:18:06,520
Like I die and leave you.

249
00:18:10,600 --> 00:18:13,420
My father loved this song as well.

250
00:18:13,920 --> 00:18:19,880
How peculiar that you would have
the same taste as Kozuki Oden.

251
00:18:20,760 --> 00:18:26,540
And now, every time I play it,
I remember my father's face.

252
00:18:31,260 --> 00:18:33,060
Your father?

253
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:40,560
Knowing that, even as I avenge his
death, I dare not show a smile.

254
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:45,960
Not in front of you!

255
00:18:47,460 --> 00:18:48,360
Captain!

256
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:51,300
Hydra!

257
00:19:08,620 --> 00:19:11,580
I don't give a crap what
you guys had planned.

258
00:19:12,380 --> 00:19:15,340
The people of this country are starving.

259
00:19:16,920 --> 00:19:18,940
You've taken enough from them.

260
00:19:20,080 --> 00:19:23,400
I'm giving this fourth gear
everything that I have left.

261
00:19:24,160 --> 00:19:28,600
And I won't stop attacking
till I put an end to you.

262
00:19:33,780 --> 00:19:37,020
I can't tell what his
attempts are coming from.

263
00:19:46,340 --> 00:19:48,320
You're leaving this country!

264
00:19:48,580 --> 00:19:49,940
I'll make sure of it!

265
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:51,860
Wano doesn't need you!

266
00:19:52,280 --> 00:19:54,140
I'm kicking you out!
